statement:
Let $(A,I)$ be a henselian pair [def-weil-pbc-henselian-terminology], $S=\operatorname{Spec}A$, $S_0=\operatorname{Spec}(A/I)$, let $f:Y\to S$ be proper [def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions], and let $Y_0=Y\times_SS_0$ with its closed immersion $i:Y_0\to Y$. Let $\mathsf{FEt}(Y)$, $\mathsf{FEt}(Y_0)$ be the categories of finite etale schemes over $Y$, $Y_0$ with $Y$-, resp. $Y_0$-morphisms, and $i^*:\mathsf{FEt}(Y)\to\mathsf{FEt}(Y_0)$, $U\mapsto U_0=U\times_YY_0$, $\varphi\mapsto\varphi_0=\varphi\times_YY_0$, the base change functor [def-weil-pbc-finite-etale-category]. Then:

(a) $i^*$ is fully faithful: for $U,V\in\mathsf{FEt}(Y)$ the map $\operatorname{Hom}_Y(U,V)\to\operatorname{Hom}_{Y_0}(U_0,V_0)$, $\varphi\mapsto\varphi_0$, is bijective (every $Y_0$-morphism $U_0\to V_0$ lifts to a unique $Y$-morphism $U\to V$);

(b) $i^*$ is essentially surjective: every finite etale $Y_0$-scheme is $Y_0$-isomorphic to $U_0$ for some $U\in\mathsf{FEt}(Y)$;

(c) hence $i^*$ is an equivalence of categories;

(d) (finite group actions lift uniquely) for a group $G$ (in the application a finite group) and $Z\in\mathsf{FEt}(Y)$, every action of $G$ on $Z_0$ by $Y_0$-automorphisms is $g\mapsto(\rho(g))_0$ for a unique action $\rho$ of $G$ on $Z$ by $Y$-automorphisms; and for every $Z'\in\mathsf{FEt}(Y_0)$ with an action of $G$ by $Y_0$-automorphisms there are $Z\in\mathsf{FEt}(Y)$ with a $G$-action by $Y$-automorphisms and a $G$-equivariant $Y_0$-isomorphism $Z_0\cong Z'$.
